sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-asterias-rubens-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-asterias-rubens-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-asterias-rubens-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Asterias rubens Turing wavelength at 115.2 µm (Holocene, Pass 1 square patch) — MorphoEval overall 84.4/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Schnakenberg kinetics on a 576.0 µm Neumann patch (five catalog wavelengths of 115.2 µm). Diffusivity ratio 7.62 is just above onset, so the p=5 mode is unstable (σ≈0.0073) and the p=4 mode is stable (σ≈−0.051). Analytical versus FTCS growth: Pearson r = 0.999817, RMSE = 0.003533, KS = 0.0833. The 2D radial-FFT wavelength is 116.4904 µm. Equal diffusion is a negative control (max numerical σ = −0.103). The Hillewaert CC BY-SA studio photograph is segmented (circularity 0.164 versus a disk at 1; foreground 0.212 versus Otsu 0.198). The GIF ends on that photograph. The photograph has no scale bar and is not a 115.2 µm micrograph. Garm & Nilsson 2014 experimented on Linckia laevigata. Overall 84.4/100 (faithfulness 82.7, reproducibility 88.5); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 90, Morphological realism / specimen match 74, Parameter expressivity 88, Morphometric validation 84, Source and data traceability 91, Code-to-model traceability 86, Reproducibility package 88. Output judged: docs/media/asterias_rubens_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-asterias-rubens-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc, image/png, 367344 B, 1632×984 px, artifact_sha256 1e0766613517dd66c929062b38c34dfa5e4ceca46265102ed100428ac39d9477 (sha256 1e0766613517dd66c929062b38c34dfa5e4ceca46265102ed100428ac39d9477), spec_fingerprint f1205721de3cf1a837201a21f488df08c3a58b144285920a89c856f2c63ab2f0. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: f1205721de3cf1a837201a21f488df08c3a58b144285920a89c856f2c63ab2f0; artifact_sha256: 1e0766613517dd66c929062b38c34dfa5e4ceca46265102ed100428ac39d9477; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/asterias_rubens_turing_wavelength_s0/asterias_rubens_specimen.jpg=7d7d25e638cab5b2..., datasets/asterias_rubens_turing_wavelength_s0/asterias_rubens_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=a5253b2ab52b4a62...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952 diffusion-driven instability and a critical wavenumber. | Schnakenberg 1979 two-species reaction with a homogeneous steady state. | Murray 1981 writes the pre-pattern wavenumber used for animal markings. | Garm & Nilsson 2014: most starfish have a compound eye at the arm tip; their navigation experiments used Linckia laevigata.; reconstructed_in_script: a=0.072, b=0.918, D_v/D_u=7.62, domain 576.0 µm, seed 3123, chosen so λ_c = 115.2 µm and only the p=5 mode is unstable. | FTCS Neumann integration, radial-FFT wavelength, diffusivity sweep λ ∝ √s, equal-diffusion ablation. | Segmentation of the Hillewaert photograph (circularity, coherency, tubercle spacing in units of arm radius).; transfer_boundary: Coat-marking reaction-diffusion is transferred to an asteroid pigment/ocellus scale. The 115.2 µm length is the catalog tier, not a published Asterias measurement. | The Linckia compound-eye result is not an Asterias rubens wavelength. | Tubercle spacing on the unscaled studio plate is dimensionless. A 0.02 arm-radius reference assumes a 5.8 mm arm and is a transfer, not a measurement of this plate.; does_not_claim: That 115.2 µm was measured as an ocellus diameter in Asterias rubens. | That the studio photograph is a micrograph at this scale, or that its pixel wavelength is 115.2 µm. | That Schnakenberg rate constants were identified in starfish epidermis. | A second, independent assessor.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Test the pentaradial body silhouette as the reaction domain on the 576 µm patch. If the arms are narrower than λ_c the mode should quench; record that control instead of forcing the mask into the production run.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'Replace the transferred 0.02 arm-radius spacing reference with a within-plate null so the tubercle metric is not anchored to an assumed 5.8 mm arm.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'No independent second assessor.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R4', 'item': 'The studio photograph has no scale bar, so absolute tubercle spacing in micrometres cannot be read from it. Keep that limit explicit.'}" ;
        pk:hasScore "0.844"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (builder-assessor, single-agent; second assessor not run)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> .
}

